Trimble UI Guidelines for React Development

Project structure:
/src
  /api        ← API service clients (Axios-based)
  /components ← Shared UI components (Buttons, Forms, Modals)
  /pages      ← Route-level views (Employees, TimeEntries, Payroll, etc.)
  /hooks      ← Custom React hooks
  /types      ← TypeScript interfaces and DTOs
  /utils      ← Helper functions
  /styles     ← Tailwind config and global styles


Standard Packages.json
 	"dotenv": "^16.5.0",
    "eslint-plugin-react-refresh": "^0.4.20",
    "framer-motion": "^12.23.16",
    "lucide-react": "^0.510.0",
    "react": "^19.0.0",
    "react-dom": "^19.0.0",

UI/UX & Tailwind Guidelines
    •Use Tailwind utility-first classes for layout, spacing, and colors.
	•Apply responsive design using Tailwind’s breakpoint system.
	•Use modal dialogs or slide-ins for create/edit flows.
	•Prefer dropdowns, toggles, and status badges for visual clarity.

API Integration Standards
	•Use Axios for all HTTP requests with a centralized api.ts or axiosInstance.ts file for base URL and interceptors.
	•Use TypeScript types/interfaces to strictly type request/response bodies.
	•Error states should be handled with user-friendly toasts, banners, or modals.
	•All forms must show client-side validation and include loading indicators.

Security and Identity
	•Authentication is handled via Trimble ID with an access token available in a secure context.
	•Attach auth tokens via Axios interceptors if applicable.
	•Do not store sensitive employee data (e.g., SSN, bank info) in browser memory.

Routing & Navigation
	•Use react-router-dom with a nested layout pattern.
	•Each page component under /pages maps to a route.
	•Use a consistent Layout.tsx with shared header/sidebar/navigation.

Testing & Dev Experience
	•Use ESLint and Prettier for consistent formatting.
	•Include basic unit tests using React Testing Library for core components.
	•Enable Hot Module Reloading in development for faster UI iteration.

Optional Enhancements
	•Use React Query or SWR for caching, revalidation, and stale state handling.
	•Include telemetry using OpenTelemetry JS SDK or LogRocket for user session diagnostics.
	•Add CSV import/export support (tax brackets, reports).
	•Use Feature Flags to toggle UI modules in dev/test environments.